<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xichong County</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xichong is a county in the north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> province in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, administered by the city of Nanchong. It is known in history as the area where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-xianzhong">Zhang Xianzhong</a>, founder of the short-lived Great Xi regime in Sichuan, was killed in battle with Qing forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hooge">Hooge</a> in early 1647, after which his army withdrew to the south.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xichong-county.jpg" alt="Xichong County" width="320" height="269" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Croquant · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_of_Xichong_within_Sichuan_(China).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
